## Usage Examples

### 1. Basic wrapping

```tsx
// App.tsx
import ErrorBoundary from "./ErrorBoundary";
import UserProfile from "./UserProfile";

function App() {
  return (
    <ErrorBoundary scope="UserProfile">
      <UserProfile userId="42" />
    </ErrorBoundary>
  );
}
```

### 2. Custom fallback UI

```tsx
<ErrorBoundary
  scope="Dashboard"
  fallback={(error, retry) => (
    <div className="error-toast">
      <p>Dashboard failed: {error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={retry}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
>
  <Dashboard />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

### 3. Sending logs to an external service (e.g. Sentry)

```tsx
import * as Sentry from "@sentry/react";

<ErrorBoundary
  scope="Checkout"
  onError={(log) =>
    Sentry.captureException(new Error(log.message), {
      extra: {
        errorId: log.errorId,
        componentStack: log.componentStack,
        timestamp: log.timestamp,
      },
    })
  }
>
  <CheckoutFlow />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

### 4. Nested boundaries for granular recovery

```tsx
<ErrorBoundary scope="Page">          {/* catches page-wide failures */}
  <Header />
  <ErrorBoundary scope="Feed">        {/* isolates feed failures */}
    <NewsFeed />
  </ErrorBoundary>
  <ErrorBoundary scope="Sidebar">     {/* isolates sidebar failures */}
    <Sidebar />
  </ErrorBoundary>
</ErrorBoundary>
```

---

## Key Design Decisions

| Concern | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Error capture** | `getDerivedStateFromError` updates state (pure); `componentDidCatch` handles side-effects (logging) |
| **Retry** | Resets all error state, triggering a fresh render of `children` |
| **Error ID** | Unique per occurrence — correlates UI reports with server logs |
| **Extensibility** | `fallback` render-prop + `onError` callback keep the core generic |
| **Accessibility** | `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"` announce the error to screen readers |
| **Details panel** | Collapsed by default; `<details>` is keyboard-accessible without JS |
